  {
    "name": "computer_js",
    "description": "Use the installed Codex Computer Use JavaScript REPL. Variables and app objects persist across calls for this OAuth connection. Browser APIs are exposed upstream but currently fail here when they require active Codex turn metadata. Call this directly; no computer_session_start or observationId is needed. First call (and after reset): execute exactly one of await cua.getState(), let app = await cua.getApp(\"AppName or bundle ID\"), let browser = await cua.getBrowser({url}), or let tab = await cua.createBrowserTab(browserId, url, options). Read the returned API instructions before continuing. Use only the documented cua APIs. After UI actions get fresh AX state before deciding the next action. Use nodeRepl.write for text and nodeRepl.emitImage for images. Results and first-use documentation pass through unchanged. This is JavaScript execution, requires computer:use and shell:execute, and is not a workspace sandbox. Local app blocks disable this tool; Codex app/browser permissions still apply. Normally returns text/images directly. If pending, use computer_js_result with its jobId, never resubmit the code. Sessions expire after 15 minutes idle or when desktop access stops. Set a unique idempotencyKey if retries might be needed; reuse exactly the same arguments/key on retry. A lost response can mean input executed: never repeat uncertain actions with a new key.",
